From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:44:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: accept an MSI affinity the AIC can't
 steer

On T8132 the AIC is an AICv2 without SIQ routing: its chip has no
affinity callback, as each interrupt goes to whichever CPU takes them.
The MSI chip passed every affinity request on to it, got -ENOSYS, and
the CPU offlining of each system sleep printed "IRQnnn: set affinity
failed(-38)" for every MSI: both root ports' PME/AER, Wi-Fi and
Bluetooth, eight to twelve lines per sleep.

Pass the request on when the parent can steer, and otherwise accept it
without writing anything (IRQ_SET_MASK_OK_DONE, so the message is not
recomposed) and report the delivery as any CPU, as the routed AICv2
chip already does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index 366d422688..fd2c27ca03 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -758,12 +758,27 @@ static void apple_msi_compose_msg(struct irq_data *data, struct msi_msg *msg)
 		msg->data += pcie->msi_vector_base;
 }
 
+/*
+ * An AIC that can't be steered (AICv2 without SIQ routing) has no affinity callback: each MSI
+ * goes to whichever CPU takes interrupts. Say so instead of -ENOSYS, which the CPU offlining
+ * of every system sleep printed once per MSI. Nothing is written, the message stays as it is.
+ */
+static int apple_msi_set_affinity(struct irq_data *d, const struct cpumask *mask, bool force)
+{
+	struct irq_data *parent = d->parent_data;
+
+	if (parent && parent->chip->irq_set_affinity)
+		return parent->chip->irq_set_affinity(parent, mask, force);
+	irq_data_update_effective_affinity(d, cpu_possible_mask);
+	return IRQ_SET_MASK_OK_DONE;
+}
+
 static struct irq_chip apple_msi_bottom_chip = {
 	.name			= "MSI",
 	.irq_mask		= irq_chip_mask_parent,
 	.irq_unmask		= irq_chip_unmask_parent,
 	.irq_eoi		= irq_chip_eoi_parent,
-	.irq_set_affinity	= irq_chip_set_affinity_parent,
+	.irq_set_affinity	= apple_msi_set_affinity,
 	.irq_set_type		= irq_chip_set_type_parent,
 	.irq_set_wake		= irq_chip_set_wake_parent,
 	.irq_compose_msi_msg	= apple_msi_compose_msg,
-- 
